### CSV import API — /api/import/**
# IntelliJ HTTP Client syntax. For the VS Code "REST Client" extension, replace the
# `> {% ... %}` handler below with `# @name login` and use {{login.response.body.token}}.
#
# mode=validate (the default) writes no business data. mode=apply writes to DB_URL.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### 0. Log in — stores the JWT in {{token}}
POST http://localhost:8080/api/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "admin", "password": "xxx" }

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.token); %}

### 1. Catalogue — which entities/columns the sync owns
GET http://localhost:8080/api/import/entities
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2. Blank template (text/csv, UTF-8 BOM)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/import/templates/houses
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. Dry run of the first sync — expect created:3, nothing written
POST http://localhost:8080/api/import/houses?mode=validate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=Boundary

--Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="houses.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

< ./houses.csv
--Boundary--

### 4. Apply it — expect created:3
POST http://localhost:8080/api/import/houses?mode=apply
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=Boundary

--Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="houses.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

< ./houses.csv
--Boundary--

### 5. Same file again — expect unchanged:3 (the idempotence check)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/import/materials?mode=apply
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=Boundary

--Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="materials.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

< ./materials.csv
--Boundary--

### 6. Sheet moved: one price edited + one new material — expect created:1, updated:1, unchanged:2
POST http://localhost:8080/api/import/materials?mode=apply
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=Boundary

--Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="materials-v2.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

< ./materials-v2.csv
--Boundary--

### 7. Now edit the app side by hand, then run #8:
#   UPDATE material SET price = 27.50
#    WHERE id IN (SELECT entity_id FROM import_ref
#                  WHERE entity_type = 'material' AND external_key = 'MAT-001');

### 8. Both sides moved — expect status:partial, conflicts:1, nothing written for MAT-001
POST {{host}}/api/import/materials?mode=apply
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=Boundary

--Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="materials-conflict.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

< ./materials-conflict.csv
--Boundary--

### 9. Sheet is stale, app wins — expect keptApp:1, unchanged:3
POST {{host}}/api/import/materials?mode=apply
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=Boundary

--Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="materials-v2.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

< ./materials-v2.csv
--Boundary--

### 10. Once more — expect unchanged:4, price still 27.50 (the two-baseline property)
POST {{host}}/api/import/materials?mode=apply
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=Boundary

--Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="materials-v2.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

< ./materials-v2.csv
--Boundary--

### 11. Row-level errors — expect failed:3, one UNKNOWN_COLUMN warning, status:partial
POST {{host}}/api/import/materials?mode=validate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=Boundary

--Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="materials-errors.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

< ./materials-errors.csv
--Boundary--

### 12. Same file, onError=abort — same report, but the file is rolled back
POST {{host}}/api/import/materials?mode=apply&onError=abort
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=Boundary

--Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="materials-errors.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

< ./materials-errors.csv
--Boundary--

### 13. Bulgarian locale: ';' separator, ',' decimals — expect unchanged:4 after #10
POST {{host}}/api/import/materials?mode=validate&delimiter=semicolon&decimal=comma
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=Boundary

--Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="materials-bg-semicolon.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

< ./materials-bg-semicolon.csv
--Boundary--

### 14a. Forgot decimal=comma — file parses, all 4 prices fail INVALID_NUMBER (status: failed)
POST {{host}}/api/import/materials?mode=validate&delimiter=semicolon
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=Boundary

--Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="materials-bg-semicolon.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

< ./materials-bg-semicolon.csv
--Boundary--

### 14b. Forgot delimiter=semicolon — header reads as one column, 400 MISSING_COLUMN
POST {{host}}/api/import/materials?mode=validate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=Boundary

--Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="materials-bg-semicolon.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

< ./materials-bg-semicolon.csv
--Boundary--

### 15. File-level failure — 400 MISSING_COLUMN, no report
POST {{host}}/api/import/materials?mode=validate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=Boundary

--Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="materials-missing-columns.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

< ./materials-missing-columns.csv
--Boundary--

### 16. Unknown entity — 400, lists what is registered
POST {{host}}/api/import/houses?mode=validate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=Boundary

--Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="materials.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

< ./materials.csv
--Boundary--
